# 0082-redesign-build-tab-colours-settings-review.patch -- after the owner's device screenshots of 0080/0081 and the read-only C# review of 0077-0081 (target/agent-work/review-cs/REVIEW.txt):
# the prototype's Build tab, a header count that cannot disagree with its rows, no blue / gradient buttons, settings only for a BUILT game, and the review's M1-M4, L1-L7.
# Applies after 0081. UNTESTED ON DEVICE AND IN THE SIMULATOR: compiled, and its pure part ran in the host harness (below).
#
# 1. BUILD TAB (the prototype target/agent-work/design/project/Main.dc.html as updated): NOW BUILDING = the build's card (stages, shader count, Pause / Resume, Cancel, the short line
#    "Continues if you leave the app.", the build screen as a small round button beside its pill) or, idle, ONE compact row ("Nothing is building" / "A build ends on Ready. Play starts the
#    game."); then READY TO BUILD (on this iPhone, not built; or built before an update or DLC was added: "Update") and IN THE CLOUD (cloud-only games, minus the hidden ones, merged as the
#    Library merges them), each with its count beside its title (BuildList, GameAppRedesign.cs); a row = a 44 pt cover (a mini cloud mark for a cloud game; initials on the name's colour), the
#    name on one line, "<size> · Not built" / "<size> · In iCloud" / "On the NAS" / "Downloading · 37 %" with a thin bar, a small amber pill (Build / Update / Download; Cancel on #25252b while it
#    downloads) and, for a game on this iPhone only, a 32 pt "…" (a built game's sheet; a not-built one's small sheet). The filter, the paragraphs, the big cards with their gradient buttons
#    and "…" squares are gone; an empty section is not shown; the queue and the shader preparation stay; the "In Files, touch and hold…" tip is the + menu's "How to add from Files"; the
#    refresh (the cloud re-listing) is a small icon. "Update & DLC" (the old cards' menu: pick files, find them in a folder, download them from the cloud) is now the menu of the game sheet's
#    "Update and DLC" row. REMOVED from the screen: "Download and build" (the prototype has Download only; the code path stays, unused) and the old "Rebuild" button of a built game's card
#    (Rebuild from scratch… stays in the sheet).
# 2. THE COUNT: the device showed "0 on this iPhone" beside a listed local game. The header and the rows came from the same facts in one call, so the likeliest cause is a refresh that stopped
#    after writing the header (Guarded catches it) and kept the rows of an earlier call; NOT REPRODUCED. Now the rows and the header are made from ONE list (BuildList.Sections / Header over
#    `games`), the header is written LAST, and the counts beside the sections are the rows' own; the Library's summary and the iPad sidebar count libShown, the listed games.
# 3. COLOURS: every primary button is the accent #efb15a with black words (Look.Capsule, Look.AccentOf no longer gives a game's own hue, GradientBackView is flat amber, Theme.Pill, ShelfButton,
#    the Mods and Saves pages' filled buttons), every secondary #25252b with a hairline; the killed-build banner's "Resume" was SystemBlue; the window's and the root view's tint are the accent
#    (the system's own alerts and menus). Cover placeholders keep initials on the name's colour (a square, not a button).
# 4. SETTINGS ONLY FOR A BUILT GAME (GameSettingsRule): a cloud-only game has Download / Cancel and Hide from the library (never Hide while it downloads), no "…", no Settings, no Choose a cover,
#    no round settings button, no inspector; a tap on its cover / card opens its menu. A game on this iPhone that is not built: no sheet, no inspector, no round button; its Build "…" (and the
#    sheet's other callers) open a small action sheet "<name>" / "Not built yet: its settings come once it is built" with "Choose a cover…", "Delete the game file", Cancel; its menu is Build,
#    Choose a cover…, Add to the build queue (kept: 0062's queue has no other entry for it now), Delete…. A paused or running build has no settings either.
#    WHAT CHANGES THE BUILD (the owner asked to be told, not to hide it silently): the game's MODS (exefs patches are applied by the build: GameAppModsUi.cs "Rebuild to apply"; crates/
#    ibuilder-pipeline mods.rs) and its UPDATE / DLC (merged by the build) are inputs of the build: with no sheet before the build, mods are reachable only once the game is built (then
#    "Rebuild to apply"); an update or DLC can still be added before the first build with + › Add a game file (it attaches by its title id). The launcher settings (frame rate, upscaler,
#    memory saver...) are read at the launch (boot.rs apply_game_settings), not by the build.
# 5. THE REVIEW (REVIEW.txt), each with a harness check where the logic is pure:
#    M1 a cancelled "Download and build" could still build: the main-thread end reads the flag again (DownloadEnd.Cancelled) before downloads.Remove and `done`, and clears it there.
#    M2 the "building" state followed `selected`: it follows the run's game (stop.Game ?? lastRunGame); a swipe or an iPad card moves the carousel's / hero's focus (FocusName) but not
#       `selected` while a run goes (so the build screen and the end notification keep the right game).
#    M3 the grid, the carousel's buttons and the Build rows were rebuilt every second during a download: rebuilt only when their key (names, states, labels, what is on: RedrawKey, no
#       percentage) changes; otherwise the bars and the words are updated in place.
#    M4 the iPad inspector stayed over Build / Settings: ShowTab closes it for any other tab.   L1 a second inspector kept its launch line.   L2 a closed sheet's launch line is dropped.
#    L3 the Certificate tile kept its ground (not a navRows entry).   L4 "On this iPhone" instead of "In On this iPhone".   L5 Cancel always reachable (Build rows; no Hide while downloading).
#    L6 Settings during a build says "A build is running" (with Watch the build).   L7 "Remove download (stays in the cloud)" only for a file the app brought from that source (its import
#       record) or of the cloud file's size (DownloadPairing), in the menu, the sheet and RemoveGameDownload itself.
#    L8 (0079's header, information): an iCloud placeholder ".X.nsp.icloud" of a Files folder is now listed as the cloud game "X.nsp" (the old listing skipped it): it appears in the Library and the
#       Build tab as a cloud game; its Download is the coordinated read (iOS downloads it first). Intended; documented here.
#
# VERIFIED (2026-11-21, M1 Pro): scripts/check-patches-apply.sh: every patch applies in order, no fuzz, no offset; the repository's patches give exactly the compiled tree (diff -r). Compile (the
#   same device project, -t:Compile): 0 errors / 40 warnings, the same per file and code as the 0079, 0080 and 0081 trees; the new texts are in GameApp.dll, the removed paragraphs are not.
#   Host harness (target/agent-work/redesign/harness82: the 0080/0081 harness with PAD81;P82 over this tree): 169 of 169 checks (the 0080/0081 ones, with 0082's menu rules, and 38 new: the
#   sections and their counts, the owner's "1 on this iPhone" case, the rows' words and buttons, the header from the same list and written last, the removed paragraphs, settings only for a
#   built game, the colours' wiring, L4, M1 late cancel, M3 keys, M2/M4/L1/L2/L3/L6 wiring, L7 pairing). 20 of 20 mutations killed (mutate82.py). The 0080 and 0081 trees still pass their
#   harnesses (118/118, 131/131).
# NOT VERIFIED: nothing ran on a device; the new rows' look, the in-place updates under a finger, the window tint on the system's alerts; the cause of the "0 on this iPhone" (not reproduced).
#
# NEW UI STRINGS (for app/verify_ipa.sh): "Nothing is building", "A build ends on Ready. Play starts the game.", "Continues if you leave the app.", "Ready to build", "In the cloud",
#   "How to add from Files", "Touch and hold the game, Share, iBuilder", "Not built yet: its settings come once it is built", "Delete the game file", "A build is running",
